` \u2014 Reference document for plugin-wide architecture, type, testing, and CLI standards (consult when enforcing rules) | - `references/python3-standards.md` \u2014 Authoritative standards and workflows; consult before applying architecture, type safety, or testing rules plugin-wide |\\n| 27 | `plugins/python3-development/skills/python3-development/SKILL.md:273` | `references/modern-modules.md` | \\\"**Module Reference**: `references/modern-modules.md` - Comprehensive guide to 50+ modern Python libraries with deep-dive documentation...\\\" \u2014 near-verbatim copy of the target's own opening line (\\\"Comprehensive guide to high-quality, Python 3.11+ compatible modules\\\") | **Module Reference**: `references/modern-modules.md` \u2014 catalog of modern Python 3.11+ libraries with patterns and trade-offs | **Module Reference**: Use `references/modern-modules.md` to find modern Python library patterns, compatibility info, and use-case guidance |\\n| 28 | `plugins/the-rewrite-room/skills/user-docs-to-ai-skill/SKILL.md:16` | `plugins/the-rewrite-room/the-rewrite-room/references/stop-slop-rules.md` | \\\"Generated prose ... MUST follow `stop-slop-rules.md`: direct claims, active voice, named actors, concrete specifics, no em dashes, no filler scaffolding.\\\" \u2014 the six rules are stop-slop-rules.md's own core rules, restated | Generated prose in `SKILL.md` and `references/*.md` must follow the anti-slop standard in `stop-slop-rules.md`. | All generated prose must comply with `stop-slop-rules.md` \u2014 consult it before writing. |\\n| 29 | `plugins/the-rewrite-room/skills/user-docs-to-ai-skill/SKILL.md:49` | `.../references/input-resolution.md` | \\\"See [input-resolution.md](...) for complete branching logic. Summary:\\\" followed by a restatement of steps 0a\u20130d that duplicates the target | See [input-resolution.md](./references/input-resolution.md) \u2014 covers all Phase 0 resolution steps and file inventory procedures. | Refer to [input-resolution.md](./references/input-resolution.md) for Phase 0 implementation details including source resolution, project-name derivation, docs discovery, and file inventory. |\\n| 30 | `plugins/the-rewrite-room/skills/user-docs-to-ai-skill/SKILL.md:126` | `.../references/workflow-identification.md` | \\\"See [workflow-identification.md](...) for detection criteria, ...\\\" immediately followed (lines 130\u2013137) by a restatement of the same detection criteria | See [workflow-identification.md](./references/workflow-identification.md) \u2014 covers Phase 1.5 workflow detection and process-siren delegation. | Refer to [workflow-identification.md](./references/workflow-identification.md) for workflow-shaped content detection, delegation prompt construction, and blocking condition responses. |\\n\\nNote on rows 18\u201325: the same \\\"full standards, graphs, and amendment process are documented there\\\" sentence is copy-pasted across 8 files pointing at `python3-standards.md`. Fixing the shared phrasing once and reapplying it everywhere it's copy-pasted may be more efficient than 8 independent edits \u2014 but check `python3-development/skills/python3-development/SKILL.md:54` (row 26) too, since it's a variant of the same boilerplate pointing at the same target from a 9th file.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Group B Related But Different Problems Surfaced By The Same Sweep 8 Findings\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nNot content duplication \u2014 these are pointers that are broken, vague, or inaccurate. Worth triaging while in the area, but need a different fix than \\\"trim to identity + trigger.\\\"\\n\\n| # | Source | Target | Current hook | Problem |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| B1 | `plugins/development-harness/skills/task-decomposition/SKILL.md:171` | `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` | \\\"For the full single-writer contract, see the `CLAUDE.md` gotcha note in `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md`.\\\" | Target is reportedly a redirect stub (`@AGENTS.md`) with no visible content of its own \u2014 verify and repoint to the actual location of the contract. |\\n| B2 | `plugins/holistic-linting/skills/holistic-linting/SKILL.md:388` | `.../references/pre-existing-issues-protocol.md` | \\\"For the full triage pipeline (groom \u2192 reproduce \u2192 plan \u2192 execute), see [Pre-Existing Issues Protocol](...).\\\" | Pointer's stage names (\\\"groom \u2192 reproduce \u2192 plan \u2192 execute\\\") reportedly don't match the target's actual flowchart stage names \u2014 verify and fix the mismatch. |\\n| B3 | `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/agent-creator/SKILL.md:18` | `.../references/agent-templates.md` | \\\"- `references/agent-templates.md` \u2014 Role-based archetypes and guidance for finding patterns\\\" | Reported: the SKILL.md's own body (lines ~62\u2013127) already contains a role-archetype table and a \\\"Find Matching Patterns\\\" section that duplicates what this reference claims to hold \u2014 check which copy should be the source of truth. |\\n| B4 | `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/agent-creator/SKILL.md:119` | `.../references/agent-templates.md#best-practices-from-existing-agents` | \\\"**See also**: `references/agent-templates.md#best-practices-from-existing-agents` for patterns like embedded examples in descriptions, identity sections, and self-verification checklists.\\\" | Reported: SKILL.md's own \\\"Agent Body Best Practices\\\" section (~441\u2013506) duplicates this content \u2014 same disposition question as B3. |\\n| B5 | `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/hook-creator/SKILL.md:39` | `.../hooks-guide/references/hooks-nodejs-extension.md` | \\\"See [hooks-nodejs-extension.md](...) for the full rule and rationale.\\\" | Vague \u2014 the preceding sentence in the source already states the rule (.cjs/.mjs, never .js); unclear what new information the pointer adds. Needs a trigger describing what's actually new in the target (e.g. rationale/history), not \\\"the full rule.\\\" |\\n| B6 | `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/optimize/SKILL.md:49` | `.../agentskills/references/best-practices.md` | \\\"Load [best-practices.md](...) before writing reference pointers \u2014 it defines the correct `Load [file](./path)` format.\\\" | Reportedly inaccurate: the target is a general skill-authoring best-practices guide, not specifically a pointer-syntax reference. Verify and correct the claim. |\\n| B7 | `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/prompt-optimization/SKILL.md:362` | `.../references/accessing_online_resources.md` | \\\"> `references/accessing_online_resources.md`\\\" | Bare file reference with no trigger or purpose statement at all \u2014 needs an actual hook added, not trimmed. |\\n| B8 | `plugins/python-engineering/skills/pre-commit/SKILL.md:693` | `.../references/pre-commit-official-docs.md` | \\\"See `references/pre-commit-official-docs.md` for complete official documentation links and detailed specifications.\\\" | Reportedly inaccurate: the target contains only external doc links, no specifications. Verify and correct the claim. |\\n</div>\\n\\n## Scope Note\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThis issue covers `AGENTS.md`, `.claude/CLAUDE.md`, all 34 `.claude/rules/*.md`, and the 107 skill/agent/command files that had at least one backtick-quoted `.md` reference (out of 341 total `SKILL.md` + agent + command files in the repo). It does not cover files with zero such references, nor pointers phrased without a backtick-quoted filename (e.g. plain-prose skill mentions like `astral:uv`).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Suggested Approach For Whoever Picks This Up\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nFor each row: re-read the current source line (content may have shifted since 2026-08-19) and the full target file, confirm the duplication still holds, then replace with one of the two suggested hooks (or a better one) \u2014 identity + trigger only, no restated content. Group A rows 18\u201326 (9 files, same boilerplate) can likely be fixed as one PR with one search-and-replace pattern. Group B